BEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-246_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"2a634c43-3190-4ea8-af29-37e3371d4223","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented as Gerrit change 2255 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2255 (commit 7c3c012b84ab). scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py (167 LOC) + 11 tests + make lint wiring. Tests pin that both sanctioned remediations pass (the ${RM_CMD:-rm} seam and a : \"${dir:?}\" guard) while the incident shape fails, and that `set -euo pipefail` alone does NOT clear the gate — set -u fires on unset, not set-but-empty, and set-but-empty is what the incident had. make lint 0, typecheck 0, current tree clean. Not closing until Verified +1 and merged.","timestamp":1787801607725277001}],"created_at":1787799893486011001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6290f9b3-ba06-42d7-9cac-4f5f76045a1c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nSplit out of `e668-b496-e264-4283` per its plan review (finding G5: that ticket bundled\ntwo independently-releasable outcomes). This is the static half.\n\nOn 2026-08-26 a pytest test `subprocess`-exec'd a real shell script that performs\n`rm -rf \"$dir\"/*`, with the path variable set to `\"\"`. The glob expanded to\n`rm -rf /*` and destroyed `/opt/homebrew` and every Homebrew-installed app in\n`/Applications`. The deeper defect is that a test asserting *\"the guard rejects an\nunsafe path\"* was able to delete anything at all: asserting on **what would have been\ndeleted** is a strictly better oracle than observing a wiped directory.\n\nThe specific offending test is not on `main` (it lives on the unmerged\n`fix-mcp-clone-blocks-boot` branch), so this gates the **class** rather than that one\nfile — consistent with how `check_raw_git_writes.py` and `check_wall_clock_asserts.py`\nalready work in this repo.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A gate flags a test that `subprocess`-execs a shell script containing an\n      unguarded destructive deletion (`rm -rf` against an interpolated variable).\n      Verified by `python scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py`.\n- [ ] The gate passes a test whose script routes deletion through an injectable seam\n      such as `\"${RM_CMD:-rm}\"`, so the recommended remediation is not itself flagged.\n      Verified by a passing fixture in\n      `tests/scripts/test_check_destructive_test_exec.py`.\n- [ ] The gate passes a script whose deletion is guarded by `: \"${dir:?}\"` plus an\n      explicit deny-list, so hardened call sites are not flagged.\n- [ ] The gate reports `path:line` for each finding and exits non-zero, matching the\n      output shape of `check_raw_git_writes.py`.\n- [ ] The gate runs in `make lint`. Verified by `make lint`.\n- [ ] Enforcement is in `make lint` (invoked by both the pre-commit hook and CI), not\n      a CI-provider-specific step (`project.portability`).\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/scripts/test_check_destructive_test_exec.py` — flags the unguarded\n  shape, passes the seamed shape, passes the `${dir:?}`-guarded shape.\n- `make lint` — the gate is wired and the current tree is clean.\n- `make typecheck` and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` — green.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- Every acceptance criterion above is checked by the command it names.\n- The current tree passes the new gate, or each pre-existing finding is fixed or\n  carries a targeted justification comment.\n\n## Notes\n\nSibling of `e668-b496-e264-4283` (the OS sandbox, the dynamic half). This gate is\nstatic analysis and cannot stop a mutation at runtime — the sandbox is the\nload-bearing control; this catches the pattern before it lands.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py","reason":"NEW: flag tests subprocess-exec-ing a script with unguarded rm -rf against an interpolated var"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_destructive_test_exec.py","reason":"flags unguarded shape; passes seamed and ${dir:?}-guarded shapes"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"wire the gate into make lint"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e668-b496-e264-4283"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"10900d82-1f53-4193-9a49-f32a911ef097","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6818-615f-555e-4bb9","ticket_type":"task","title":"Gate tests that subprocess-exec scripts with unguarded destructive deletion","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6a5285f3-9343-4948-905f-838fa6dff1d1","4ad9ae3c-df36-4c90-b602-6652ba9db1e7","6290f9b3-ba06-42d7-9cac-4f5f76045a1c","7a20e7a2-a849-467a-b81a-d2e9b59538e0","10900d82-1f53-4193-9a49-f32a911ef097","4c26040e-ae3f-4095-b4c3-5b58baba3b7c","92a7ba49-782a-427c-92d3-90e1f696b8e9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787801607725277002,"uuid":"a3a9d260-6ce3-4e25-9864-22156099441c"}